# Never translate line endings, anywhere in this repository.
#
# The test corpus is byte-sensitive by design: §12.2's gate asserts that parsing
# and re-rendering a dictionary reproduces it exactly, and tests/corpus/corpus.json
# records a sha256 of every vendored file. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this a checkout there silently rewrites every LF
# to CRLF — the corpus hashes stop matching, and the one gate that guarantees the
# editor never corrupts a user's case fails for a reason that has nothing to do
# with the editor.
#
# Applied repository-wide rather than to tests/corpus alone. A CRLF shell script
# or a CRLF workflow file is its own kind of broken, and this project has no file
# that benefits from translation.
* -text

# The vendored corpus is reference data, not source. Marking it so keeps it out
# of diff noise and language statistics.
tests/corpus/** linguist-vendored
docs/PRD-v1.0.md linguist-documentation
